FINDINGS Quick #C1284, line from 937daa1167afae9791d91f11cdb25ee04ee6ec75. F1 (regression): openDecision only ends on the owner's 'Chose ...', so a decision whose thread is closed or resolved without a pick stays pinned with live Choose buttons in both threadHtml modes (acts and decide). Probed on this tip: Manager 'No longer needed' with resolved:true -> resolved true, pinned, buttons A,B; the owner's own resolve in words -> same; the owner's closer 'thanks' (threadOpen false via ownerCloser) -> pinned, buttons A,B; Manager's later 'Withdrawn: I'll pick A myself' -> pinned, buttons A,B. A click sends a stale 'Chose A' that reopens a closed thread. Before this commit the buttons went in all four cases. Fix: openDecision returns null once the thread is resolved (threadResolved) or a later message closes it (resolved:true, or an owner message ownerCloser accepts), plus tests for each of the four. The CSS look is the Designer's call.
